        "Ask the product supplier to clarify unclear intended-use information before treating a purchase as a settled installation choice. Do not assemble a trial arrangement, connect multiple sets or operate a damaged item to show how it behaves. Product identification and an explanation of the intended use are enough for the initial discussion. A concern about damaged equipment is a safety matter, not a reason to experiment while waiting for a permanent-work quote.",
