        "If you already know of a damaged fitting, an electrical symptom or a desired installation change at the destination, list that as separate work. State which premises the concern belongs to and whether you can arrange authorised access. Do not enter before you have access, open meter equipment or operate switches to find out whether the property is ready. A repair enquiry can describe an existing observation without turning moving preparations into an inspection.",
        "Ask the electrical provider what its visit will cover, then keep any repair findings with that work record. If another party must resolve a supply issue, establish who will follow it up; do not assume completing a private repair opens an energy account or authorises energisation. Similarly, account confirmation is not an assessment of the home's wiring. The move can involve both processes without either provider's confirmation silently replacing the other's responsibilities.",
